Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Andrew MURFIN
Author-Workplace-Name: Birbeck College
Author-Name: Keith COWLING
Author-Workplace-Name: University of Warwick
Title: Price Formation and Import Penetration in U.K. Manufacturing Industry
Abstract: We proceed by discussing the theoretical and empirical literature. It is suggested that the existing empirical results may have several possible alternatives explanation and that U.K manufacturing industry may not be subject to significant foreign price competition. It is argued that the conventional hypothesis that imports are independent of the domestic oligopoly structure is not altogether convincing. We pursue a specification which is an adaptation of that conventional view of import price competition. The results obtained in the estimation of this model, while not conclusive, do give grounds for doubting the conventional hypothesis.
Length: 27
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
