Author-Name: Pierre-Henri DERYCKE
Author-Workplace-Name: University of Paris X-Nanterre and GDR EVER (CNRS)
Title: Road pricing-Analysis and policies (A historical perspective)
Abstract: This paper explains how road pricing and toll charge theory appeared and evolved on the basis of contributions from the French engineer-economist school, from Dupuit to Allais, and of Anglo-Saxon theories inspired by Pigou and Vickery on decongestion tolls and network tools.
