Author-Name: Luca LAMBERTINI
Author-Workplace-Name: ENCORE, Faculty of Economics and Econometrics, University of Amsterdam
Author-Name: Raimondello ORSINI
Author-Workplace-Name: Department of Economics, University of Bologna
Title: Positional effects, product quality and regulation in duopoly
Abstract: We investigate positional effects in a vertically differentiated duopoly, evaluated against the first best. Positional concerns distort the allocation of consumers across varieties, as well as the average quality. If the external effect is sufficiently relevant, the resulting welfare loss is increasing in the extent of the externality itself. The beneficial effect of regulation through a minimum quality standard is analysed.
Classification-JEL: D62, L13, L51
Keywords: Positional externality, status siiking, vertical differential, quality standard
Length: 16
