Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: François FONTAINE
Author-Workplace-Name: Université Strasbourg 3, BETA-CNRS and IZA
Title: Do workers really benefit from their social networks ? 
Abstract: This paper provides a simple matching model in which unemployed workers and employers can be matched together trough social network or trough more formal methods of search. We show that this crowding-out effect may be socially costly. For that reason, a policy increasing the social capital of the disadvantaged workers can increase the unemployment rate and decrease worker’s output.
Classification-JEL: E24,J64, J68, Z13
Keywords: economic policy, matching, social networks, unemployment
Length: 28
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
