Author-Workplace-Name: Centre d’Etudes de l’Emploi and CES (CNRS and, Université Paris I)
Author-Name: Héloise PETIT
Author-Workplace-Name: Centre d’Etudes de l’Emploi and CES (CNRS and, Université Paris I)
Author-Name: Antoine REBÉRIOUX
Author-Workplace-Name: Economix (CNRS, Université Paris X)
Title: The Stock Market and Human Resource Management : Evidence from a Survey of French Establishments
Abstract: This article examines the influence of equity ownership structure (stock market listing and identity of shareholders) on human ressource management practices. The empirical analysis uses the 2004-2005 Workplace Industrial Relations Survey (REPONSE survey), based on a sample of 2930 establishments with 20 employees or more, representative of the French private sector. Our findings confirm the importance of listing and, to a lesser extent, of the identity of shareholders as determinants of human resource management pratices, considering temporary work arrangements (agency work, fixed-term contracts and sub-contracting), pay policy (wage levels and use of variable pay) and training expenditures.
Classification-JEL: G34, J3, M5
Keywords: Corporate Governance, Ownership of equuity capital, human ressource management
Length: 21
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
