Author-Name: Fabian Bergès
Author-Workplace-Name: Toulouse School of Economics (GREMAQ-UMR)
Author-Name: Claire Chambolle
Author-Workplace-Name: INRA and Ecole Polytechnique
Title: Threat of Exit as a Source of Bargaining Power
Abstract: This article analyzes a simple two period model where two homogenous manufacturers compete to supply a monopolist retailer. We show that if manufacturers are vulnerable (i.e if they are likely to exit the market in case of insufficient orders in the first period) they may exploit their threat of exit to capture the whole first period industry profit. Indeed, the retailer will accept to pay the high price to the manufacturers in order to secure upstream competition in the second period. Results are robust under different market structures or contract types.
Classification-JEL: L14, D21, Q12
Keywords: Bargaining power, market entry, vertical contract
Length: 15
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
