Author-Workplace-Name: Toulouse School of Economics (LERNA)
Author-Name: Isabelle Péchoux
Author-Workplace-Name: Toulouse School of Economics (ARQADE)
Title: Domestic Effects of Environmental Poclicies with Transboundary Pollution
Abstract: We model environmental interaction among countries as a policy game where government in each country use quotas or taxes as a strategy variables. The environmental policy has a triple role to play : targeting domestic emission, providing strategic advantages for domestic firms  and targeting imported pollution. Using a multi-sector economic model, we show that, besides the well-known inefficiencies arising at the international level, the environmental policy may lead to purely domestic inefficiencies.
Classification-JEL: F18, Q20, Q28
Keywords: Environmental policy, Transboundary Pollution, Multi-sector Model
Length: 21
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
