Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Marie-Laure CABON-DHERSIN
Author-Workplace-Name: Ecole Normale Supérieure de Cachan
Author-Name: Rim LAHMANDI-AYED
Author-Workplace-Name: Ecole Polytechnique de Tunisie
Title: R&D Organization: Cooperation or Cross-Licensing?
Abstract: Under the Cross-Licensing system (CL), firms are allowed to trade non cooperatively the results of R&D efforts, and compete in the innovation and production stages. First, the paper proposes a simple modeling of this system. Second, a relevant comparison is made with the Cartelized Research Joint Venture (RJV), the form of R&D cooperation recognized to be the best one.
We prove that the Cross-Licensing system may be socially better than the Cartelized RJV. In terms of antitrust policy, for firms, the most favorable collusion mode is Joint Exploitation. We prove that firms are equally tempted by this mode, whether they are under CL or under Cartelized RJV.
Classification-JEL: C72;L24; D23
Keywords: Cross-Licensing, R&D cooperation, Cartelized Research Joint Venture, R&D spillovers, Efficiency, Antitrust policy
Length: 22
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
