Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Jacques H. DRÈZE
Author-Workplace-Name: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Center for Operations Research and Econometrics (CORE)
Author-Name: Alain DURRÉ
Author-Workplace-Name: Université Catholique de Lille, IESEG-School of Management
Author-Name: Jean-François CARPANTIER
Author-Workplace-Name: University of Luxembourg, CREA
Title: Fiscal Integration and Growth Stimulation in Europe 
Abstract: With the current sovereign debt crisis, the incompleteness of economic integration in the Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) has become patent, leading to an intense debate among academics and policy makers. Much of the debate concerns fiscal rules and austerity measures, both of which weigh on growth prospects. In this paper we look at the main structural shortcomings of EMU through the lens of general equilibrium theory. We address two issues (international sharing of macroeconomic risks and coordinated growth stimulation) which are at the heart of the sustainability of EMU. We propose : (A) a specific scheme for mutual insurance of macroeconomic risks ; (B) locating responsibility for demand policies at the EMU level, with ambitious investment programs (public, or fiscally-neutral private) as main instrument.
Classification-JEL: E24, E63, H63
Keywords: General equilibrium model, Risk sharing, Growth simulation, Fiscal integration, Indexed bonds
Length: 40
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014021
Creation-Date: 2014-06-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014021

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Vincent MAURIN
Author-Workplace-Name: European University Institute
Author-Name: Jean-Pierre VIDAL
Author-Workplace-Name: European Central Bank and Centre d’Economie de la Sorbonne
Title: Monetary Policy Deliberations : Committee Size and Voting Rules
Abstract: How large should a monetary policy committee be ? Which voting rule should a monetary policy committee adopt ? This paper builds on Condorcet’s jury theorem to analyse the relationships between committee size and voting rules in a model where policy discussions are subject to a time constraint. It suggests that in large committees majority voting is likely to enhance policy outcomes. Under unanimity (consensus) it is preferable to limit the size of the committee. Finally, supermajority voting rules are social contrivances that contribute to policy performance in a more uncertain environment, when initial policy proposals are less likely to be correct, or when payoffs are asymmetric.
Classification-JEL: D71, D78, D81, E58
Keywords: Monetary policy, Collective decision-making, Optimal comittee size, Voting Rules
Length: 36
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014022
Creation-Date: 2014-06-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014022

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Raphaële PRÉGET
Author-Workplace-Name: LAMETA, INRA UMR 1135
Title: Does the competition structure impact the performance of multi-unit auctions ? An experimental investigation 
Abstract: Competition in a multi-unit auction is measured both by the number of bidders and by the relative size of their demands, compared to the number of units on sale. For the same degree of competition (identical aggregate demand and supply), we can observe different demand structures. Do they have an impact on the auction efficiency and revenue-raising properties ? It is essential to understand better the impact of competition structure on performance in order to draw recommendations for the design of multi-unit auctions. Theoretical results demonstrate on a simple case contrasting a uniform-price auction of two bidders with a demand of 6 units each, and an auction of 6 bidders with a demand of two units each, that there are multiple equilibria leading to different performance outcome. Experiments are conducted to compare the performance of these two auctions. Results support that with a constant competition degree, the seller gets higher expected revenue with a lower variance when he faces a large number of bidders with small individual demands. We show that this result is attained with no significant effect on allocative efficiency.
Classification-JEL: C92, D4, D44
Keywords: Experiments, Multi-unit auction, Competition structure
Length: 24
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014023
Creation-Date: 2014-06-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014023

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Jean-Marie LE PAGE
Author-Workplace-Name: University of Paris II Panthéon Assas
Title:  Growth-Employment Relationship and Leijonhufvud's Corridor
Abstract: Since 2008, the euro area unemployment rate has increased constantly, while this economy’s GDP was the same at the end of 2012 as it was in 2008. The recent trend of aggregate economic activity in this area illustrates the risk that an economy leaves its stability corridor, in which it usually progresses in a cyclical way, to enter an area of turbulence. In this area, the automatic stabilizers have weak feedback forces. To examine this kind of situation in a theoretical framework, this paper presents a model that relies both on Leijonhufvud’s corridor and on Harrod’s instability principle. This model allows a threshold to be defined beyond which the economy runs the risk of entering a cumulative process of simultaneous declines in growth and employment. However, the existence of such a process requires unemployment to have a sufficiently direct effect on the growth in aggregate demand, as seems to be the case nowadays.
Classification-JEL: B22, E12, E24
Keywords: Growth-employment relationship, Economics dynamics, Instability principle, Corridor
Length: 13
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014024
Creation-Date: 2014-06-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014024

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Jean-Pierre LAFFARGUE
Author-Workplace-Name: University of Paris 1, Maison des sciences économiques
Title: Tourism as an Automatic Stabilizer
Abstract: We explore how the damaging effects of a sudden stop in capital inflows to a small open economy can be dampened by an increase in spending by foreign tourists. Tourism reduces the relative importance of the traded good sector, which is especially sensitive to a rise in the cost of foreign capital. Moreover, the lower prices of non-traded goods attract more tourists whose spending slows down the price deflation and increases still more the relative importance of the non-traded good sector. This stabilizing effect increases with the price elasticity of the tourist demand function that is when the services to tourists supplied by the economy have better substitute in other countries.
Classification-JEL: F11, F32
Keywords: Tourism, Sudden stop, Automatic stabilizer
Length: 15
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014031
Creation-Date: 2014-09-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014031

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Alain BÉRAUD
Author-Workplace-Name: Université de Cergy-Ponthoise, THEMA
Title: La formulation du modèle keynésien et le choix de l'unité de mesure
Abstract: Cet article analyse la façon dont Keynes et les keynésiens posèrent la question du choix de l’unité de mesure des agrégats macroéconomiques. Soulignant les rapports étroits qui existent entre les cours que Keynes professa entre 1933 et 1935 et les diverses versions du modèle IS-LM, il montre que les problèmes naissent de la façon dont Keynes avait abordé cette question. Raisonner sur la valeur monétaire des agrégats conduit à dichotomiser le modèle et ne permet pas d’analyser correctement l’interdépendance entre le marché du travail d’une part et les marchés des biens et de la monnaie d’autre part. Dans le modèle ainsi formulé, il est impossible d’étudier de façon rigoureuse les effets d’une variation du salaire monétaire et l’on est conduit à penser, à tort, qu’il existe nécessairement un équilibre de plein emploi si le taux de salaire monétaire est flexible.
Classification-JEL: B22, E12
Keywords: Keynes, IS-LM, Unité de mesure
Length: 29
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014032
Creation-Date: 2014-09-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014032

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Nada BEN ELHADJ
Author-Workplace-Name: Université de Tunis, ISG
Author-Name: Rim LAHMANDI-AYED
Author-Workplace-Name: Université de Carthage, ESSAI
Author-Name: Didier LAUSSEL
Author-Workplace-Name: Université Aix-Marseille, GREQAM, CNRS & EHESS
Title:  Advertising Spillovers and Market Structure
Abstract: In this paper we characterize the equilibrium of a duopoly market which exhibits advertising spillovers. Interestingly, we prove that the relevant distinction is not between pure positive and pure negative advertising spillovers but between strong positive spillovers and weakly positive or negative spillovers. Moreover, we prove that, depending on the extent of advertising spillovers and the agency advertising cost, we may obtain at equilibrium either two active advertisers or only one advertiser that may even push its rival out of the product market. Thus advertising and the spillovers induced from it may be a source of a monopoly situation, hence an asymmetric outcome may result from an initially symmetric situation.
Classification-JEL: L11, L13, M37
Keywords: Advertising spillovers, Quantity competition, Agency cost
Length: 47
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014033
Creation-Date: 2014-09-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014033

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Sophie LECOSTEY
Author-Workplace-Name: University of Caen Basse-Normandie, CREM - UMR CNRS 6211
Title:  A Model of Adverse Promotion
Abstract: This paper considers the incentive role of promotion. It presents a simple theoretical model in which candidates for promotion are uncertain about the type of evaluator mandated by the Organization to review them. Adverse promotion is then shown to occur, the term “adverse” meaning here unfair and/or inefficient. Unfairness is tied to the possible existence of an evaluator enjoying power. Indeed, in the separating Perfect Bayesian Equilibrium such an evaluator promotes a worker from among the less competent candidates in order to signal his type and thence to induce further candidates to court his favour. Inefficiency arises with both types of evaluator (the power-liking and the ethically-acting) but is different in nature : either it is tied to courting behaviour of workers, or it is due to the discouragement of some workers. The role played by competition between heterogeneous workers is then discussed and some remedies are suggested.
Classification-JEL: M51
Keywords: Taste for power, Courting, Discouragement, Promotion
Length: 16
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014041
Creation-Date: 2014-12-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014041

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Aline BRANCHE-SEIGEOT
Author-Workplace-Name: Institut de Recherche en Sociologie et Économie de l’Éducation (IREDU)
Title: La maitrise du français écrit par les primo-arrivants : une analyse des performances productives par frontière stochastique
Abstract: Cet article vise à déterminer les facteurs susceptibles d’expliquer le niveau de maîtrise du français écrit par les primo-arrivants en âge de travailler, sachant que peu de recherches ont été réalisées en France à ce sujet. L’originalité de cet article réside dans l’estimation d’une frontière stochastique de production afin d’expliquer les scores en français écrit des primo-arrivants (considérés comme producteurs de leurs propres compétences) et leurs performances productives. Les principaux résultats mettent en avant que la langue maternelle, l’âge au moment de l’immigration, le diplôme de la mère et la vie sociale sont des éléments qui influencent l’efficacité de cette production. Ils jouent un rôle essentiel dans la capacité des primo-arrivants à utiliser efficacement leur durée de présence en France et leur durée d’éducation scolaire, considérées comme les principales ressources dont disposent les primo-arrivants pour produire de la compétence dans la langue du pays d’accueil.
Classification-JEL: I21, J15, J24
Keywords: Frontière stochastique de production, Primo-arrivants, Compétence de base
Length: 27
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014042
Creation-Date: 2014-12-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014042

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: Yankou DIASSO
Author-Workplace-Name: Université de Strasbourg, BETA UMR 7522 CNRS
Title:  Dynamique du prix international du coton : aléas, aversion au risque et chaos
Abstract: Alors que la récente flambée des cours des matières premières ravive le débat sur l’explication endogène versus exogène des fluctuations, nous montrons dans cet article que les deux phénomènes sont conjointement en œuvre dans la dynamique des prix mensuels du coton. L’application des outils de détection du chaos (dimension de corrélation, exposant Lyapunov) sur la série des prix montre certes l’existence d’une instabilité propre au fonctionnement même du marché, mais le test d’effet ARCH confirme également celle d’une part d’aléa. Aussi avons-nous fait appel à un modèle combinant processus chaotique et stochastique (Mackey-Glass – EGARCH) inspiré de la théorie des agents hétérogènes pour reproduire les caractéristiques des prix. Nos résultats suggèrent que la dynamique complexe des prix pourrait avoir pour origine l’hétérogénéité des formes d’anticipation des agriculteurs.
Classification-JEL: C22, E32, O13
Keywords: Prix du coton, Fluctuations endogènes, Anticipations hétérogènes, Modèle Mackey-Glass-EGARCH
Length: 33
Series: UNIVERSITE CATHOLIQUE DE LOUVAIN, Institut de Sciences Economiques
Number: 2014043
Creation-Date: 2014-12-01
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:ctl:louvre:2014043

